        </div><div class="article-template__content page-width page-width--narrow rte scroll-trigger animate--slide-in">
          <div class="rocket-shopify-article lngvty-article" style="max-width:880px;margin:0 auto;color:#181818;font-family:'Avenir Next',Avenir,'Century Gothic','Trebuchet MS',sans-serif;font-size:17px;line-height:1.75;letter-spacing:.15px;">

    <p style="max-width:760px;margin:0 0 24px;color:rgba(24,24,24,.68);font-size:20px;line-height:1.5;letter-spacing:.2px;">
        A serum can make skin look more luminous by improving hydration, tone and texture over weeks, but it cannot deliver the instant, airbrushed finish that filter-style marketing promises.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:0 0 38px;padding:20px 22px;border-left:4px solid #181818;background:#FFFEF3;">
        <p style="margin:0;color:#181818;">
            <strong style="font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.5px;">Quick answer:</strong>
            The best serum for glowing skin keeps the skin well hydrated, supports an even-looking tone and works alongside daily sunscreen. Look for a water-binding ingredient, ceramides for the barrier, and niacinamide or a stable form of vitamin C for tone. Expect change over weeks rather than overnight, and be cautious about any serum that promises an instant filter finish. Use it daily on damp skin, followed by moisturiser and morning sunscreen.
        </p>
    </div>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Skin looks glowing when light bounces off a smooth, evenly coloured, well-hydrated surface. Most marketing sells something else: a sheen that photographs well for a few hours, or a before-and-after taken in flattering light. Once you know what a real glow is made of, it gets much easier to pick a serum that earns its place in your routine.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        What a real glow is made of
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Three things do most of the work, and a good serum can influence all three.
    </p>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Hydration.</strong> The outer layer of skin holds water through a mix of barrier lipids and water-binding molecules, and when that system is disturbed the skin turns dry and flaky.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/14728698/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>1</sup></a> Dry, flaky skin rarely looks luminous.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Even tone.</strong> Marks left by sun and old breakouts break up the colour of the surface. In a trial in Japanese women, niacinamide reduced facial hyperpigmentation and increased skin lightness after four weeks of use, compared with a plain moisturiser base.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12100180/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a> Topical vitamin C is also reported to reduce melanin formation.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Smooth texture.</strong> A healthy barrier keeps the surface even. Ceramides are lipids that occur naturally in skin and help it hold moisture in, which is why many hydrating serums and moisturisers include them.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24656726/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a>
</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Where filter-skin marketing goes wrong
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        A filter smooths skin by editing the image. A serum can only work on the skin itself, and skin changes slowly. Four promises deserve a careful read:
    </p>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Instant glow.</strong> A sheen that sits on the surface disappears when you wash your face. It tells you nothing about what the serum does to your skin over time.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Poreless, airbrushed skin.</strong> Pores are a normal part of skin. A serum can help skin look smoother, but it cannot remove them.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Overnight transformation.</strong> The skin changes in the research above showed up over weeks of daily use, not after a single night.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12100180/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>The highest percentage wins.</strong> For vitamin C in particular, researchers describe finding a stable, well-absorbed formula as the main challenge, so a bigger number on the label does not guarantee better results.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a>
</li>
    </ul>

    <div style="margin:42px 0;padding:30px 26px;background:#181818;color:#FFFFFF;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#B87330;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2.2px;text-transform:uppercase;">
            The LNGVTY system
        </p>
        <h2 style="margin:0 0 12px;color:#FFFFFF;font-size:31px;line-height:1.15;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.8px;">
            Choose by skin concern
        </h2>
        <p style="margin:0 0 24px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.7);font-size:15px;line-height:1.6;">
            Dull, dehydrated or tight-feeling skin points to the serum below.
        </p>

