    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        What to look for on the label
    </h2>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Read the ingredient list for a few jobs instead of chasing one hero ingredient:
    </p>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>A water-binding ingredient.</strong> Glycerin, hyaluronic acid and similar ingredients help the surface of the skin hold water.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Ceramides.</strong> They are part of the lipid layer that keeps water in, and skincare brands add them to support the barrier.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24656726/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>4</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>A tone ingredient.</strong> Niacinamide and a stable form of vitamin C both have published evidence for a more even-looking tone, and each works over weeks.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12100180/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a><a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a>
</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>A simple, calm formula.</strong> Patch test first and add one new product at a time, so you know what is helping and what is irritating.</li>
    </ul>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        <a href="/products/deep-hydration-glow-serum-30ml" style="color:#181818;text-decoration-color:#B87330;text-decoration-thickness:2px;text-underline-offset:4px;">Deep Hydration, Glow Serum</a> is built around those jobs. It combines niacinamide, a stable form of vitamin C (3-O-ethyl ascorbic acid), saccharide isomerate, five ceramides with cholesterol and a set of peptides, and it works as the one active step in the routine. In the serum's own clinical study on Indian skin, glow increased by 35.2% at four weeks, and individual results may vary.
    </p>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        How to use a glow serum
    </h2>

    <ol style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:24px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Cleanse</strong> with a mild cleanser.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;"><strong>Apply 3 to 4 drops on damp skin.</strong></li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;"><strong>Moisturise.</strong></li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Use sunscreen in the morning.</strong> Dermatologists say that effective care for dark marks begins with sunscreen, which also protects the tone you are working on.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a>
</li>
    </ol>

    <p style="margin:0 0 22px;">
        Patch test before first use. If you are pregnant or breastfeeding, check with a doctor first. The serum is designed as the active step, so there is no need to layer another brightening product on top.
    </p>

    <div style="margin:34px 0;padding:24px 26px;border-top:1px solid #B87330;border-bottom:1px solid #B87330;background:#FFFEF3;">
        <p style="margin:0 0 7px;color:#B87330;font-size:12px;line-height:1.2;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:2px;text-transform:uppercase;">Keep in mind</p>
        <p style="margin:0;color:#181818;">
            A glow built on hydration and tone changes gradually. Photograph your skin in the same daylight every two weeks, so you judge the result by what your skin looks like and not by how it feels in the first hour.
        </p>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        What to expect, and when
    </h2>

    <ul style="margin:0 0 22px;padding-left:22px;">
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>The first days to two weeks.</strong> Skin that felt tight or dry may start to feel more comfortable first, because hydration is the quickest thing to change.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Around four weeks.</strong> This is the point at which the serum's own study measured glow. Individual results may vary.</li>
        <li style="margin:0 0 10px;">
<strong>Several months.</strong> Dark marks that sit a few shades above your natural skin colour usually fade within 6 to 12 months once the cause is dealt with.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a> A serum can support that process, but it cannot rush it.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        A quick guide to glow claims
    </h2>

    <div style="margin:24px 0 34px;overflow-x:auto;border-top:2px solid #181818;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.25);">
        <table style="width:100%;min-width:620px;border-collapse:collapse;text-align:left;font-size:15px;line-height:1.55;">
