    <h2 style="margin:56px 0 18px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        Frequently asked questions
    </h2>

    <div style="border-top:2px solid #181818;">
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can a serum give glowing skin overnight?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">No. A serum can leave skin feeling smoother the same day, but changes in tone and radiance build over weeks of daily use, alongside sunscreen.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12100180/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a><a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a></p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Is vitamin C necessary for glow?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">No. Hydration and barrier support matter at least as much, and niacinamide has its own evidence for a more even-looking tone.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12100180/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>2</sup></a> Vitamin C is a useful addition when it comes in a stable formula.<a href="https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/29104718/" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>3</sup></a></p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Can I use a glow serum with my other actives?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Deep Hydration, Glow Serum is designed to be the active step in the routine, with vitamin C and niacinamide already in the formula, so layering more actives is usually unnecessary. If you use a prescription treatment, check with your doctor before adding anything new.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Is it suitable for oily skin?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Deep Hydration, Glow Serum is formulated for all skin types, and the routine continues with a moisturiser and sunscreen either way. Patch test before first use, and introduce it on its own for a week so you can see how your skin responds.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">Do I still need moisturiser and sunscreen?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Yes to both. Moisturiser follows the serum in the routine, and sunscreen each morning protects the tone you are working on.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a></p>
        </div>
        <div style="padding:22px 0;border-bottom:1px solid rgba(24,24,24,.2);">
            <h3 style="margin:0 0 8px;color:#181818;font-size:21px;line-height:1.3;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.25px;">How long before I see a difference?</h3>
            <p style="margin:0;">Skin that felt tight or dry may feel more comfortable within the first couple of weeks. In the serum's own clinical study on Indian skin, glow was measured at four weeks, and individual results may vary. Visible changes in tone take longer.<a href="https://www.aad.org/public/everyday-care/skin-care-secrets/routine/fade-dark-spots" rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank"><sup>5</sup></a></p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2 style="margin:52px 0 16px;color:#181818;font-size:34px;line-height:1.12;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-1.15px;">
        References
